" The one name here with a dash in it, and so the one that cannot be a w rule.
" A w rule is looked up in an index of the line built a character class at a
" time, and "E-Mail" is three runs of the line -- "E", "-" and "Mail" -- so the
" whole of it is never a key. Written out, it is the same \< \> a w rule wraps.
syntax			E-Mail					n/\<E-Mail\>
