syntax	Comment			n/\"\".*
" The block markers take the quote in front of them, so that they beat the
" comment rule below on the tie: both start at column 0, and the earlier rule
" wins one of those.
syntax	PreCondit		n/^\"\=begin\s\+files\s*=.*
syntax	PreCondit		n/^\"\=end\s\+files
syntax	PreCondit		n/^\"\=begin\s\+suffixes\s*=.*
syntax	PreCondit		n/^\"\=end\s\+suffixes
" A comment on a line of its own. Only that: a rule file writes \" inside its
" patterns all the time -- m/\".*[^\\]\" is an ordinary String rule -- and a
" rule that took any quote for the start of a comment would paint every one of
" those as one. 154 of the comments in syntax/ are on their own line and 18 are
" not, so this is the side to be wrong on.
syntax	Comment			n/^\s*\".*
syntax bolic	text	w/bolic
