" Every other colour is drawn in itself, and white cannot be -- on the window's
" own background it would be the one name in the list that is invisible. Now
" that a rule can say what goes behind it, it can be drawn in itself after all.
syntax	white on gray	w/white
" A colour written out rather than named. #rrggbb is what the rule files use
" for a background, none of the sixteen names being pale enough to read a line
" of text off.
syntax	Constant		n/#\x\x\x\x\x\x
" rc files color define
syntax	link			SetSpecial			bold	text
syntax	link			ColonCommand				red
syntax	link			SetParam					fuchsia
syntax	link			SetShortParam		bold	fuchsia
syntax	link			SetCommand					green
syntax	link			SetShortCmd			bold	green
syntax	link			UnsetCommand				maroon
syntax	link			UnsetShortCmd		bold	maroon
syntax	link			SetTerminal			bold	gold
syntax	link			SetKeyboard			bold	silver
syntax	SetSpecial		w/SetSpecial
" What follows "syntax": the commands, and the "on" that introduces a
" background. Below the link above, because a rule naming a group the editor
" has not been given yet is refused. "link" is also an HTML tag and an HTML
" attribute, so two lines of html.jvsyn get it as well -- the same bargain the
" group names here already make, and worth it for the same reason.
syntax	SetSpecial		w/link/clear/load/color/dump/crchar
syntax	SetSpecial		w/on
